 { Black is in some trouble since his king would be checked once the g-pawn queens. Letelier found the only defence. } 1... { -KEY- } Kd4 $1 ( { a) The natural } 1... c4 $2 { loses after } 2. bxc4 bxc4 ( { a1) or } 2... Kxc4 3. g5 { and White queens with check; } ) 
3. g5 c3 4. g6 c2 5. g7 c1=Q $11 6. g8=Q Kd4 ( { a2) or } 6... Kd6 7. Qd8 { and 8.Qc8+; } ) 
7. Qd8 $1 Kc3 ( { a3) the desired } 7... Ke3 { fails to } 8. Qg5 ) 
8. Qc7 Kb2 9. Qxc1 Kxc1 10. Ke4 $1 Kd2 11. Kd4 { (obstruction) } Ke2 12. Kc5 ) 
 ( { b) As for } 1... b4 $2 2. g5 c4 { , White wins by } 3. g6 $1 ) 
2. g5 c4 3. bxc4 b4 $1 { So that the pawn queens with check. } ( 3... bxc4 $2 4. g6 c3 5. g7 c2 6. g8=Q $11 c1=Q $11 7. Qd8 $1 { returns to 1...c4? above. } ) 
4. g6 ( { In the game Fischer erred incredibly with } 4. c5 $4 { and had to resign after } b3 5. c6 b2 6. c7 b1=Q 7. Ke6 Qb7 8. Kd7 Kd5 9. g6 Qc6 10. Kd8 Qd6 { . } ) 
b3 5. g7 b2 6. g8=Q b1=Q+ { Black saves a draw. } 
 *

