 { In this tense pawn ending Black has just advanced ...b5-b4, and White must now play his cards right. } 1. { -KEY- } axb4 $2 { This capture yields Black an extra tempo in the pawn race. } ( { Correct was } 1. Kh6 $1 c4 2. e7 Kxe7 3. Kg7 c3 4. bxc3 bxc3 5. f6 Ke6 6. f7 c2 7. f8=Q $11 c1=Q $11 { with a draw - Andersson. } ) 
cxb4 2. Kh6 a3 3. e7 Kxe7 4. Kg7 ( { Unfortunately for White, after } 4. bxa3 bxa3 5. Kg7 a2 { , Black queens with check. } ) 
axb2 5. f6+ Kd7 $1 ( { Andersson has seen that from here the king will support a future exchange of queens on e7. Instead after } 5... Ke6 $2 6. f7 b1=Q $11 7. f8=Q $11 { White manages to stay in a queen endgame, with good drawing chances. } ) 
6. f7 b1=Q 7. f8=Q { White had probably pinned his hopes on defending this queen ending a pawn down; however... } Qg1+ $1 ( { After } 7... Qg1 8. Kh6 ( { and } 7... Qg1+ 7. Kh7 Qh2 9. Kg7 Qg3 10. Kh7 Qh4 11. Kg6 Qe4 12. Kh6 Qe6 { leads to the same thing } ) 
Qe3 $1 { Black manages a queen exchange either on e8 or e7, so White resigned. } ) 

 0-1

