 { Black has an extra tempo in this pawn race, but how to take advantage of it? } 1... { -KEY- } Kxf4 $1 ( { After } 1... Kxh4 $2 2. Kxa4 { , followed by 3 b4, White queens as well. } ) 
2. Kxa4 g5 3. hxg5 hxg5 $1 { The pawn should queen on g1. Here White resigned; let's see why: } 4. b4 g4 5. b5 Ke5 $1 { By approaching the b-pawn with his king, Black aims at forcing the white king to a7, so that the g-pawn queens with check. } 6. b6 Kd6 7. Kb5 g3 8. Ka6 g2 9. b7 Kc7 $1 10. Ka7 g1=Q+ { Black wins - Smyslov. } 
